{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488380-fan-splat-idea-bonded-the-union","id":1488380,"title":"Fan Splat Idea: Bonded: The Union","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-29T12:29:33-07:00","id":1488380,"title":"Fan Splat Idea: Bonded: The Union","content":"This idea is mainly for fantasy settings where there are things like giant boars, wyverns, and dragons, but I could see it working in Chronicles of Darkness if you have a VERY creative GM. Basically, it's people who have a supernatural bond with some sort of monster. It's a bit like animal companions from Druids and Rangers only on a larger scale.<br /> <br /> The theme of it is that of having an incredibly close bond, not necessarily a positive bond (though it could be) but a close one, with some sort of entity or entities that makes you fundamentally linked to each other. As such, I thought that the morality equivalent would be:<br /> <br /> Bond:<br /> Bond starts at 5. It cannot be bought but must be raised through actions. Bonds 8, 9, and 10 give a +1, +2, and +3 bonus to issuing commands to the monster respectively. Bonds 3, 2, and 1 give a -1, -2, and -3 penalty to issuing commands. At Bond 0, the monster will not obey its commander.<br /> <br /> These commands would be issued through the Animal Ken skill, and I had some ideas for modifiers on Bond rolls; though, I don't have many at this point:<br /> Things that can increase bond: Spending time with the monster, doing something in the monster\u2019s benefit,<br /> Things that can decrease bond: Using the monster as a sacrifice or meat shield,<br /> Suggested Modifiers:<br /> You had no choice in your action +1 for decrease and -1 for increase.<br /> <br /> As for the power stat, I thought it could be potency. Except it wouldn't be your potency the PC is increasing, but the monster their connected to's. This would work similar to the COFD or Hunter the Vigil rules on monster creation; though, some adjustments would need to be made for game balance. Here are some of the concepts I'm floating around with it:<br /> Increasing the Potency requires 5 experience points. At Potency 3, 6, and 9 you can get an additional monster. A separate Potency and bond track is kept for them.<br /> When a monster gets above Potency 5, its supernatural bond with the rider allows them to raise their stats above 5.<br /> <br /> In terms of supernatural abilities, the bonded would have their own. Only these would be based around the connection to their monster:<br /> Abilities:<br /> (maybe have to buy them separately for separate monsters?)<br /> <br /> Communication:<br /> 1: Commanding a monster is now an instant action.<br /> 2: Your monster has an innate sense of when you are in mortal danger.<br /> 3: You can command your monster telepathically, regardless of distance.<br /> <br /> Power:<br /> 1: You can give your Willpower points to your monsters, limited by normal Willpower expenditure rules.<br /> 2: Your monsters can give their Willpower points to you, limits from potency applying.<br /> 3: You can use one of the monsters\u2019 dread powers as your own.<br /> <br /> Coordination (maybe a fighting style instead of a power?):<br /> 1: When riding a monster, all rolls with the drive skill are instant actions.<br /> 2: In battle, you and your monster may act at the same time, using the higher of your or your monster\u2019s initiative roll.<br /> 3: Once a day, when fighting alongside your monster, you may replace one of your attributes with your monster\u2019s for a single roll. Or maybe: When riding or fighting alongside your monster in some way, you both gain +1 Defense and a +1 Bonus to attack rolls. Or something else.<br /> <br /> Some non-combat ability and a few others, of course.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about a lot of this, but I think I'm on the right track by deciding on the general theme first and making the splat rules based around it. What does everyone think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T12:31:11-07:00","id":1488382,"title":"","content":"Niiiiiiiiice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T15:29:48-07:00","id":1488606,"title":"","content":"After some thinking about things, I made an updated version of this:<br /> You command your monsters with animal ken rolls and ride them with the drive skill. Each command requires an action and must be issued through vocal cues.<br /> The bonded and the monster may give each other points of Willpower with the usual restrictions on maximum Willpower and the amount that can be spent per turn. Hunters always have the Bonded condition with their monster.<br /> <br /> Morality Stat: Bond:<br /> Bond starts at 5. It cannot be bought but must be raised through actions. Bonds 8, 9, and 10 give a +1, +2, and +3 bonus to issuing commands to the monster respectively. Bonds 3, 2, and 1 give a -1, -2, and -3 penalty to issuing commands. At Bond 0, the monster will not obey its commander.<br /> <br /> Things that can increase bond: Spending time with the monster, doing something in the monster\u2019s benefit,<br /> Things that can decrease bond: Using the monster as a sacrifice or meat shield,<br /> Suggested Modifiers:<br /> You had no choice in your action +1 for decrease and -1 for increase.<br /> <br /> Power Stat: Potency:<br /> This is the Potency of the monster you command. It would use Hunter: The Vigil or normal COfD rules for the stats. Increasing the Potency requires 5 experience points. At Potency 3, 6, and 9 you can get an additional monster. A separate Potency and bond track is kept for them.<br /> When a monster gets above Potency 5, its supernatural bond with the rider allows them to raise their stats above 5.<br /> <br /> Merit: Kinship: 1 to 5:<br /> Each dot of this merit allows the Rider to designate someone as family. Their monster will view that person as family and will treat them as such.<br /> <br /> Bonded Abilities (3 or 4 XP? Get three at Character Creation):<br /> Shared Vision:<br /> You can enter a trance where you see through your monster\u2019s eyes, hear through their ears, and smell through their nose. During this time, your mind is within your monster and you don\u2019t need to speak to give it commands.<br /> <br /> Telepathic Mind:<br /> You can command your monster telepathically. Commanding them is an instant action, and they can sense whenever you are in mortal danger.<br /> <br /> Combat Training:<br /> When in battle, you and your monster act at the same time, on whichever of you gets the higher initiative roll. Additionally, you both get 1 extra defense and a +1 bonus to all combat rolls when fighting alongside each other.<br /> <br /> Physicality of the Beast:<br /> You may replace one of your attributes with your monster\u2019s. This lasts 1 scene and does 1L damage to you per turn it\u2019s active for. Alternatively, you may get 1 of the monster\u2019s dread powers for the scene and only take bashing damage. These can be stacked for 1L and 1B damage per turn. If this stat is stamina, it doesn\u2019t increase your maximum HP.<br /> <br /> Pained Sacrifice:<br /> By spending a point of willpower, you or your monster can take the full damage of one hit for the other. This is done after the damage is calculated, and any armor you or your monster have doesn\u2019t reduce it further.<br /> <br /> Protective Bond:<br /> When your monster has one of its three rightmost health boxes filled, you get a bonus equal to the amount of boxes filled to all rolls towards protecting your monster or killing whoever harmed it. The same is true in reverse with your monster getting those bonuses when you\u2019re injured.<br /> <br /> Transport Training:<br /> When you\u2019re riding on your monster, double the weight it can carry based on its Strength.<br /> <br /> Monstrous Aid:<br /> By spending a point of Willpower, you may give your monster one of your skills for a scene, provided that it is capable of understanding and acting upon that skill. Maybe give bonus on teamwork rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T21:12:24-07:00","id":1488760,"title":"","content":"This Bonded fansplat idea sounds very cool! Say, what would be the Bonded's equivalent of stuff like Clans and Covenants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:29:31-07:00","id":1488848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1488380-fan-splat-idea-bonded-the-union?p=1488760#post1488760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Bonded fansplat idea sounds very cool! Say, what would be the Bonded's equivalent of stuff like Clans and Covenants?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks and for the X and Y things, I'm not sure if they need it. They might be more like Hunters with various different groups rather than things like Clans and Covenants. Or maybe neither. The core theme of Bonded is the bond between the players and the specific monsters they've bonded with. So, I'm not sure if associating them with a larger group would be fitting. However, if other people think differently and have ideas, I'd be happy to hear them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}